Me koik maletame kuupaeva 15. september 2008. Paeva, mil pankrotistus uks neljast Wall Streeti suurest investeerimispangast, Lehman Brothers. See, kaimasoleva sajandi maailma rahaturge enim mojutanud sundmus oli taaskord toestuseks, et voimatu voib muutuda valtimatuks koigest uhe nadalavahetusega. Mainitud kuupaevale jargnenud globaalne, doomino efekti meenutav sundmustejada on meie silme all lahti rullunud kui erakordselt heatasemeline Hollywoodi monetaartragoodia. Ajalehtede eepilis-dramaatilisi pealkirju lugedes oleme korduvalt tundnud, et elame erakordsel ajal. Hardo raamat on heaks kiirkursuseks maailma majanduslikku, rahanduslikku ja poliitilisse ajalukku toestamaks, et ei ole midagi uut siin paikese all. Koik uus on araunustatud vana voi vahemasti sama nahtuse moodne muteerunud vorm. Niivord vana, et me kas ei suuda voi ei taha seda maletada, veel vahem tunnistada. Lopuks taandub koik korgele seatud otsustajate isiku omadustele, veendumustele ja nende baasil tehtud valikutele. Poliitiline loom ja majanduslik inimene elab meis koigis, soltumata meie uhiskondlikust positsioonist voi aravalitusest.
Kaesolev raamat ei andesta pealiskaudset lugemist. Tegemist on tugeva toimelise majandus-poliitilise kontsentraadiga, mida on soovitav tarbida vastavalt retseptile. Hardo valjendusviis on isikuparane, paralleelide tabamine kordumatu.
Viljar Arakas"‰
·Sabrina would just love to zap Libby Chessler clear into the next galaxy...but then, what else is new? After all the work Sabrina has put into planning the Harvest Moon dance, Libby is trying to step in and take over. So what if a hip TV station is doing a news feature starring Libby? And so what if she's gotten the station to donate funds for the dance? Does that give her the right to run the whole show?
Just about everyone seems to think so. Even Harvey is bewitched by Libby, the TV star! But Sabrina isn't giving up yet. After all, she's got Magic on her side.
What could possibly go wrong?
Don't ask."Á
‰Roman Holiday "Let the magic guide you."
-- Edward Spellman
If Sabrina Spellman can't open mysterious antique gold locket and release the power trapped within, a family secret will be lost forever. "The secret to the locket lies in Rome," says her father. So, with stowaway Salem in her backpack, Sabrina heads for Italy and the Eternal City of Rome.
Once there, she meets Paul, the gorgeous American photographer who grabs her before she falls into the famous Trevi fountain. And in her charming "pensione," Sabrina finds an unexpected roommate: Gwen, a British witch with a talking hamster named Stonehenge. Together, Sabrina and Gwen set out to solve the mystery of the locket -- a story of love and betrayal that began centuries ago...."	
